FILE: K:\Minecraft Narrative Studio\.agents\skills\story-architecture\SKILL.md
---
name: story-architecture
description: Build or audit a causal, character-driven Minecraft story architecture without imposing a universal plot formula.
---

# Story Architecture

## Required inputs

Approved concept and research, `studio/writing-doctrine.json`, relevant postmortems, and current production constraints.

## Outputs

`.studio/internal/story/story-model.json`, `causal-spine.csv`, `sequence-outline.csv`, `beat-sheet.csv`, `scene-cards.csv`, `relationships.csv`, `information-map.csv`, `setup-payoff-ledger.csv`, `story-outline.md`, `treatment.md`, and `continuity-bible.md`.

## Method

1. Separate chronological story, causal plot, and audience presentation.
2. Reconfirm the audience promise and thematic conflict from approved concept evidence. Propose changes explicitly; do not silently rewrite them.
3. Build the character system around want, need, fear, belief, limitation, strategy, contradiction, boundary, pressure point, relationship function, and agency.
4. Design active opposition, layered stakes, final choice, climax mechanism, final state, and final image before filling the middle.
5. Create the minimum causal spine. For every major event record causes, actor, goal, decision, consequence, state change, information effect, later dependencies, counterfactual result, deletion impact, and production note.
6. Expand into sequences and beats. Each sequence records a temporary objective, strategy, location, complications, reversal/outcome, and resulting story state. Each beat states who acts, what they attempt, what interferes, what changes, and why the next beat follows.
7. Track audience knowledge, questions, expectations, emotional orientation, and character knowledge in the information map.
8. Register every major setup and its planned payoff, reinterpretation, cut status, or intentionally open serial reason.
9. Record relationship dynamics when more than one principal character exists, then build scene cards. Require purpose, entry/exit states, earned story value, and production requirements. Treat objective, obstacle, turn, and outcome as useful but flexible diagnostics.
10. Choose and justify the architecture that fits the material. Three acts, a midpoint, a protagonist arc, sequence counts, and opening/closing-image symmetry are optional.
11. Write an emotion-driven treatment without changing the approved graph, then make Minecraft mechanics, geography, inventory, construction, travel, and world rules alter choices, strategy, conflict, or climax.
12. Run `mcstudio story-audit <slug> --scope outline`, then separate failures, warnings, and creative recommendations.

## Gate test

Major events form a valid causal graph; references resolve; audience information is controlled; setup obligations are accounted for; the climax follows from earlier choices and rules; Minecraft is causally necessary; continuity can be filmed; and human judgement—not a formula—has selected the structure.

FILE: K:\Minecraft Narrative Studio\.agents\skills\audience-information-design\SKILL.md
---
name: audience-information-design
description: Design suspense, curiosity, surprise, dramatic irony, mystery, and fair reveals through explicit audience and character knowledge states.
---

# Audience Information Design

## Output

`.studio/internal/story/information-map.csv`, relevant setup/payoff rows, and information sections in scene cards and script.

## Method

For every important question or fact record what the audience knows, expects, fears, and hopes before delivery; what relevant characters know; how the information is shown; what changes after delivery; and which earlier setups make the reveal fair.

A twist should be difficult to predict but clearer in retrospect. Do not create surprise by making necessary evidence impossible to infer. Distinguish deliberate uncertainty from accidental confusion.

## Effects

Use suspense for uncertain consequential outcomes, curiosity for missing causes or explanations, dramatic irony when the audience knows more than a character, and mystery when the audience reconstructs concealed events, motives, identities, or rules.

FILE: K:\Minecraft Narrative Studio\.agents\skills\scene-design\SKILL.md
---
name: scene-design
description: Design or audit scenes for dramatic change, information control, visual value, subtext, and solo production feasibility.
---

# Scene Design

## Output

Rows in `.studio/internal/story/scene-cards.csv` and corresponding stable sections in `03-script/script.md`.

## Method

Record entry state, purpose, story value, production requirements, and exit state for every scene. Use objective, obstacle, tactics, turn, and outcome where they clarify the scene engine; treat them as diagnostics rather than mandatory laws.

Track literal words, speaker objective, fear, tactic, concealed information, relationship status, power shift, and subtext for important dialogue. Begin near meaningful friction and leave after decisive change unless atmosphere, ritual, anticipation, contrast, aftermath, setup, or thematic value justifies more duration.

## Audit question

If the scene is removed, what later event, character understanding, emotional progression, world knowledge, setup, payoff, visual rhythm, or production transition becomes weaker or impossible?

FILE: K:\Minecraft Narrative Studio\.agents\skills\continuity-control\SKILL.md
---
name: continuity-control
description: Track canon, timeline, geography, props, world rules, character knowledge, relationships, setups, and version impact across a video or series.
---

# Continuity Control

## Source of truth

`.studio/internal/story/story-model.json`, `continuity-bible.md`, `information-map.csv`, `setup-payoff-ledger.csv`, and stable IDs in causal, beat, scene, shot, capture, and edit files.

## Method

Record rules before exceptions. Maintain chronological timeline separately from audience presentation. Track location graph, travel constraints, inventory/resources, injuries, abilities, relationship states, and who knows each fact at every important point.

For every exceptional Minecraft/world rule, record who knows it, how the audience sees proof, what it permits, what it prevents, and what happens when it is broken.

A proposed canon change must record reason, affected upstream decision, downstream script/shot/set/capture/edit/caption/packaging impact, uncertainty, and human decision. Reopen before editing locked evidence.

## Failure condition

Do not patch a contradiction by adding unexplained lore. Return to the earliest invalid assumption, causal link, world rule, or knowledge transfer.


